@namespace DotNetCloud.Modules.Video.UI

@*
    Help content for the Video module.
*@

<div class="help-content">
    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Overview</h2>
        <p>DotNetCloud Video lets you browse, play, and manage your video library directly from your browser. Stream your personal video collection anywhere, with series support, subtitles, and transcoding.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Browsing Your Library</h2>
        <p>Use the sidebar to switch between <strong>Home</strong> (recently added videos), <strong>Library</strong> (series first, then standalone videos), <strong>Series</strong>, <strong>Favorites</strong>, and <strong>Library Settings</strong>.</p>
        <p>Use the <strong>search bar</strong> to find specific titles. Cards show thumbnails, title, duration, file size, and resolution.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Series</h2>
        <p>Series are detected automatically when scanning your library. Files named like <code>Show.Name.S01E01.mp4</code> or organized in <code>Show Name/Season 01/</code> folders are grouped together. Open a series to browse its seasons and episodes.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Playback</h2>
        <p>Click a video to start playback in the built-in player, which supports play/pause, seeking, volume control, fullscreen, and playback speed adjustment.</p>
        <p>Supported formats include <strong>MP4</strong>, <strong>MKV</strong>, <strong>AVI</strong>, <strong>MOV</strong>, <strong>WebM</strong>, and <strong>FLV</strong>. The player shows codec and container information and can display available <strong>subtitles</strong>; content is delivered directly, remuxed, or transcoded as needed. Watch progress and history are tracked.</p>
        <p><strong>Favorites:</strong> Use the star button in the player to favorite a video and find it again in the <strong>Favorites</strong> section.</p>
        <p><strong>Metadata:</strong> Use <strong>Edit metadata</strong> from the player to correct a video's title or other details.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Library Settings</h2>
        <p>Open <strong>Library Settings</strong> to configure and scan your video library. Resetting the collection removes indexed metadata (videos, collections, subtitles, watch progress, watch history, shares) — your actual video files are not affected.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Tips &amp; Tricks</h2>
        <ul class="help-tips">
            <li>Name series files consistently (<code>Show.Name.S01E01.mp4</code>) so they group into series automatically.</li>
            <li>Adjust playback speed for educational or lecture content.</li>
            <li>Search across your entire library to find videos instantly.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
